# Word-list exceptions for `repo.spelling`. The file list is decided by
# scripts/check_spelling.sh, not here — see that script's header for why a
# bare `codespell .` could not scan `.claude/` and `.github/` at all.
#
[codespell]
# `skip` intentionally absent: the scan is an explicit file list, so there is
# no directory walk left to prune.
# Each of these is a deliberate exception, not a silenced nuisance:
#   bloc     the state-management library the Flutter rules mandate
#   blocs    its plural, which appears in prose about the client
#   pres     the Mermaid node id for `presentation/*` in the layers diagram;
#            renaming it would break the diagram, not fix a typo
#   re-use   ISO 27001 Annex A control A.7.14 is titled "Secure disposal or
#            re-use of equipment". The Statement of Applicability quotes it
#            verbatim, and a compliance document that paraphrases a control
#            title no longer cites the standard. Never "fix" this one.
#   homestate  codespell reads the Bloc class `HomeState` (frontend/…/home)
#            as the misspelling of "home state"; it is a type name.
#   hace     Spanish. Specs quote the TL's own words verbatim when a defect
#            was reported in them — "no hace nada" is the report, and a
#            paraphrase in English would be a second-hand account of the
#            only evidence a UI defect had. codespell reads it as "have".
ignore-words-list = assertIn,asend,bloc,blocs,crate,ist,nd,te,som,ba,fo,requestor,socio,pres,re-use,homestate,hace
